{
  "notes": {
    "event": "The React callback belongs to a React-only API or is named after the React convention while the element dispatches the documented minerva-* event (onDropdownVisibleChange / onClose -> minerva-open-change, onOptionClick / onItemSelect -> minerva-select, Pagination onChange -> minerva-page-change); onPaletteChange follows ConfigProvider's setPalette(), which <minerva-config> does not have (the palette is its attribute).",
    "react-only": "React composition or styling hooks with no custom-element equivalent (ReactNode props without a slot of the same name are slots named differently, e.g. startIcon -> slot start; per-part style objects are ::part() selectors; data props that are children elements in HTML, e.g. KeyValueEditor entries -> value).",
    "wc-only": "Element vocabulary: string attributes replacing ReactNode props (heading, label, description, text), attributes replacing React context / provider values (locale, dialogRole, closeLabel...), state the element reflects for styling (collapsed, mobile, open on items), native-like properties React gets from the DOM element it renders (required, disabled, readOnly, placeholder, minLength, maxLength, autocomplete, href, target, rel, download, type, value)."
  },
  "differences": {
    "minerva-alert": ["react-only expanded", "react-only role", "react-only rounded", "wc-only alertRole", "wc-only collapsed", "wc-only heading", "wc-only square"],
    "minerva-app-shell": [
      "react-only labels",
      "wc-only closeNavigationLabel",
      "wc-only collapseLabel",
      "wc-only collapsed",
      "wc-only disableFloatingLabel",
      "wc-only enableFloatingLabel",
